  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "baseline",
      "name": "Baseline (deadline budget, one retry layer)",
      "description": "The document as drawn: 600 req/s, a quarter of them checkouts. Every request succeeds. p95 is about 200 ms; a checkout, which calls pricing, inventory, the database and the cache in turn, takes about 230 ms at p95. The busiest part is the BFF at about half its CPU.",
      "overrides": []
    },
    {
      "id": "pricing-hangs",
      "name": "Pricing answers 5 s late (40\u201370 s), as drawn",
      "description": "Chaos: from 40 to 70 s every call to pricing takes 5 s longer (a latency fault on its link, as a stuck connection pool or an overloaded node would cause). Orders gives up after 800 ms, so every checkout in the window fails within a second, and the mobile app's one retry fails the same way. Order history is untouched: every read succeeds, and success in the window is 75.5%, which is the reads. The deadline budget keeps the failure where it started.",
      "overrides": [
        {
          "target": {
            "kind": "workload"
          },
          "path": "faults",
          "value": [
            {
              "id": "pricing-hangs",
              "kind": "latency",
              "target": "route-pricing",
              "startS": 40,
              "durationS": 30,
              "extraMs": 2500,
              "label": "pricing answers 5 s late"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "retry-every-hop",
      "name": "Pricing late, retries at every hop",
      "description": "The same hang with three attempts at every hop (the ingress, BFF \u2192 orders, the pricing route, orders \u2192 inventory; 100 ms backoff) on top of the app's own retry. The design review flags it before the run: up to 54 attempts reach pricing per checkout. Pricing was only slow; the retries overload it. It receives about four times its normal traffic (593 req/s against 152) and turns away 62% of it. Requests stay in flight so long that the ingress's circuit breaker (Envoy's default, 1,024 per target) opens, and order-history reads start failing too. Success in the window falls to 67.9%.",
