      "id": "inverted",
      "name": "Pricing late, inverted timeouts",
      "description": "The same hang with the deadlines turned around: the services wait longer than the apps (the ingress back to Envoy's 15 s default, BFF \u2192 orders and the pricing route 10 s), while the apps keep 8 s and 5 s. Checkouts now complete, in about 5 s. The web shop waits for them (its p95 becomes 5.1 s); the mobile app gives up at 5 s and retries while its first attempt carries on. 21% of the work inventory completed was for attempts the app had already abandoned (the wasted-work finding): about 2,900 checkouts went through after the app had shown an error, and only the idempotency key stops the retry placing a second order. Orders' threads are held 5 s per checkout, its queue overflows and the ingress's circuit breaker opens, so reads fail too: 70.6% succeed in the window.",
