      "id": "breaker",
      "name": "Pricing late, no timeout, circuit breaker",
      "description": "The same missing timeout with a circuit breaker on the pricing route: its Envoy answers 503 at once when 64 calls are already in flight to pricing (Envoy's default is 1,024). At most 64 of orders' threads wait on pricing, every other checkout fails immediately, and order history is untouched again: every read succeeds and 74.6% of requests succeed in the window, as with the timeout. A breaker caps how much of a pool one dependency can take; it is the backstop for a timeout someone forgot.",
